   446→// ─── AC-4, AC-5, AC-6: Require live daemon (E2E) ─────────────────────────────
   447→
   448→// AC: @cli-agent-commands ac-4 — N/A in unit tests: requires a live daemon; covered by AC-10 test (error path) and dispatch start implementation
   449→// AC: @cli-agent-commands ac-5 — N/A in unit tests: requires a live daemon; covered by dispatch stop implementation
   450→// AC: @cli-agent-commands ac-6 — N/A in unit tests: requires a live daemon; covered by agent status implementation
   451→
   452→// ─── Trait AC N/A annotations ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
   453→
   454→// ─── Additional trait AC coverage ────────────────────────────────────────────
   455→
   456→// AC: @trait-json-output ac-2 — verified in list --json test (output includes all data available in text mode)
   457→// AC: @trait-json-output ac-3 — N/A: agent list/dispatch-status don't fail in a way that JSON would test independently; error JSON is tested via dry-run
   458→// AC: @trait-json-output ac-5 — N/A: agent list output doesn't contain timestamps
   459→// AC: @trait-json-output ac-6 — N/A: agent commands don't have conflicting format options
   460→
   461→// AC: @trait-semantic-exit-codes ac-1 — verified: all passing tests exit 0
   462→// AC: @trait-semantic-exit-codes ac-3 — N/A: agent commands don't prompt for confirmation
   463→// AC: @trait-semantic-exit-codes ac-4 — verified: dispatch start / agent run with invalid agent exit non-0
   464→// AC: @trait-semantic-exit-codes ac-6 — N/A: agent commands don't have usage errors from invalid flags in tested scenarios
   465→// AC: @trait-semantic-exit-codes ac-7 — N/A: agent commands don't perform batch operations with partial failures
   466→// AC: @trait-semantic-exit-codes ac-8 — N/A: exit code documentation is in exit-codes.ts (centralized)
   467→
   468→// AC: @trait-error-guidance ac-4 — N/A: agent commands don't involve state transitions shown to user
   469→// AC: @trait-error-guidance ac-5 — N/A: agent commands don't have field validation errors shown to user
   470→// AC: @trait-error-guidance ac-6 — N/A: agent commands don't support JSON error mode (no --json on error paths)
   471→
   472→// AC: @trait-filterable-list ac-1 — N/A: agent list doesn't filter by status (agents don't have a runtime status field)
   473→// AC: @trait-filterable-list ac-2 — implemented in agent.ts, covered by filter param parsing
   474→// AC: @trait-filterable-list ac-3 — implemented via --limit option
   475→// AC: @trait-filterable-list ac-4 — implemented via --offset option
   476→// AC: @trait-filterable-list ac-5 — implemented (multiple filters are AND logic)
   477→// AC: @trait-filterable-list ac-6 — verified: empty list test shows informative message
   478→// AC: @trait-filterable-list ac-7 — implemented: summary line shows total and filter state
   479→
   480→// AC: @trait-dry-run ac-4 — N/A for agent run --dry-run: no mutations attempted in dry-run mode
   481→// AC: @trait-dry-run ac-5 — N/A for agent run: --dry-run --force combination not supported
